    verification touchedReceiptIsContentKeyedPerBinaryReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "f05af0b4-2916-43b5-b03a-3ac58e65a791"; :>> title = "Sprint 706 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Three passes (D0172). Correctness: a green is recorded only when contentkey::compute before and after the run are equal (touched.rs run(): held is Some only on equality), so a tree that moved mid-run records nothing and the next run re-executes; a red drops its binary's row (merge_observed removes every ran entry and re-adds only the greens); the skip needs the code key equal and, for a self-reading binary, the tree key too - a .tracking edit alone reruns exactly the self-reading set, shown in the integration test. Honesty: the receipt names ran and skipped apart and the summary says 'skipped, observed green at this content', never 'passed'; --no-receipt and KEEL_NO_RECEIPT=1 run everything; the observation table is inside .keel/metrics/, now a protected surface, so no hand edit produces a skip. Scope: the perf report short-circuits when Model::build was never called, so contentkey:compute's phase is not printed - the overhead is measured as the whole third run instead, 1.5 s wall including the eol census; the synopses of cliSuite and cliLand still do not name the skip (issue538, tracked, not patched)."; }
