    verification touchedReceiptIsContentKeyedPerBinaryRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "787fe3f1-d3fc-43f2-80a8-e2e74f31ffd1"; :>> title = "Sprint 706 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Avoidable issues scanned; findings are tracked items, not prose. Finding one: the first real-tree run was red for a reason outside the code - KEEL_PERF=1 in the suite's environment reached every keel the tests spawn, and three binaries that parse JSON or diff output failed on the perf lines; issue539, resolver dcTouchedRunScrubsPerfFromTheChildEnv (scrub the variable from the cargo child, report to stderr). Finding two: the D0108 supersede route does not exist for CliCommand facts because cli-surface-declared compares every authored fact to the mirror; issue538, resolver dcCliFactsOwnedByARetiredActorAreSupersedable (a guard change, so its Decision will be held for the human). Finding three: the fixture failure mode of D0474 is silent - a tree that always moves under cargo never skips and never says why; the integration test asserts a skip so the class is covered, and the real-tree third run (nothing to execute) is the census that the repository's ignores are sufficient today. Closed in-sprint: gitfacts::head_sha memoises per process, which would have keyed a mid-run commit under the old HEAD - contentkey reads HEAD live and its doc says why."; }
